  "obstruction_arity": {
    "statement": "An admissible clique yields only the four-term S-unit relation (a+b)+(c+d)=(a+c)+(b+d). Height theorems (Baker-Gyory, abc) are three-term. For four terms only solution COUNTS exist (Evertse-Schlickewei-Schmidt, exp(O(k))), and Erdos-Stewart-Tijdeman show counts cannot be pushed below exp(c(k/log k)^{1/2}).",
